#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0333 expect=skipped domain=DM
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when a Findings About dataset name begins with "FA", is longer than two characters, and the characters following "FA" do not match the two-character code of a domain present in the study.
#note "⚠ THIS SCENARIO CHANGED VERDICT (noViolation -> skipped) AND THAT IS THE POINT. CDISC-CG0333 is scoped `Domains.Include: [ALL]` + `include_split_datasets: true`; the flag used to be applied ADDITIVELY (mirroring Python `_handle_split_domains`), under which the flag was a no-op against `ALL` and the rule ran on every dataset in the study. It is now a CONJUNCTIVE gate — in scope iff the dataset matches Include AND is a split — so `ALL` + `true` means SPLITS ONLY. That is what this rule has always authored in its own `Source` block: Condition 'Dataset split by parent domain and dataset name length > 2 and dataset name begins with FA'. DM carries DOMAIN=DM, so its data-derived base equals its name, it is not a split, and it is now out of scope BEFORE the check is reached. The original intent of this scenario — an in-scope dataset whose name does not start with FA does not fire — is preserved by the sibling -valid-LBHM scenario. DM is not a Findings About dataset (name does not start with FA), so the rule would not fire even if it ran."
dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023
---
